      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved, understandable version of the test.Now I'll compile-check the test.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version removes dead code (unused fields, phantom `__super_*` method stubs, and helper methods not called by the test), trims imports to only what's needed, and adds a brief class-level and method-level comment that explains the Cartesian product empty-collection contract — making the test's intent immediately clear without changing any runtime behavior."
